---LdapConfig contains all the parameters for connecting to LDAP servers.
---@class gcp.unstable.file_v1beta1.LdapConfig
---@field usersOu? string Optional. The users Organizational Unit (OU) is optional. This parameter is a hint to allow faster lookup in the LDAP namespace. In case that this parameter is not provided, Filestore instance will query the whole LDAP namespace.
---@field domain? string Required. The LDAP domain name in the format of `my-domain.com`.
---@field servers? gcp.unstable.file_v1beta1.StringList Required. The servers names are used for specifying the LDAP servers names. The LDAP servers names can come with two formats: 1. DNS name, for example: `ldap.example1.com`, `ldap.example2.com`. 2. IP address, for example: `10.0.0.1`, `10.0.0.2`, `10.0.0.3`. All servers names must be in the same format: either all DNS names or all IP addresses.
---@field groupsOu? string Optional. The groups Organizational Unit (OU) is optional. This parameter is a hint to allow faster lookup in the LDAP namespace. In case that this parameter is not provided, Filestore instance will query the whole LDAP namespace.

